                                        "sense_id": "173424be-ce97-3564-bafa-078a722f638f",
                                        "entry_id": "04086950-ae50-3a25-ae86-88ccb97823f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a range of polymers containing amide (or peptide) repeat units; examples include proteins and nylon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0384441e-941b-42af-b39d-83f7e10144bd",
                                                "sense_id": "173424be-ce97-3564-bafa-078a722f638f",
                                                "text": "For eons, the debris has contained the same things — flecks from plant and animal carcasses, feces, mucus, dust, microbes, viruses — and transported the ocean’s carbon to be stored on the seafloor. Increasingly, however, marine snowfall is being infiltrated by microplastics: fibers and fragments of polyamide, polyethylene and polyethylene terephthalate. And this fauxfall appears to be altering our planet’s ancient cooling process."
